{"id": "EUVD-2026-5861", "enisaUuid": "88b5a2ed-f40a-33b5-978a-fb825f199f87", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndpaa2-switch: add bounds check for if_id in IRQ handler\n\nThe IRQ handler extracts if_id from the upper 16 bits of the hardware\nstatus register and uses it to index into ethsw->ports[] without\nvalidation. Since if_id can be any 16-bit value (0-65535) but the ports\narray is only allocated with sw_attr.num_ifs elements, this can lead to\nan out-of-bounds read potentially.\n\nAdd a bounds check before accessing the array, consistent with the\nexisting validation in dpaa2_switch_rx().", "datePublished": "2026-02-14T16:27:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:25:34", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77611cab5bdfff7a070ae574bbfba20a1de99d1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34b56c16efd61325d80bf1d780d0e176be662f59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f89e33c9c37f0001b730e23b3b05ab7b1ecface2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2447edc367800ba914acf7ddd5d250416b45fb31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b381a638e1851d8cfdfe08ed9cdbec5295b18c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31a7a0bbeb006bac2d9c81a2874825025214b6d8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pmxm-x3p3-w327", "CVE-2026-23180"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09f89167-e2e4-3c88-86f1-2cbfdbfdf528", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.70"}, {"id": "178112c5-2a77-3740-b0a2-84e723975ba9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "2c6b0253-b2ee-39b9-9fca-26a93057ac10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24ab724f8a4661b2dc8e696b41df93bdc108f7a1 <31a7a0bbeb006bac2d9c81a2874825025214b6d8"}, {"id": "367c3fbd-68e0-36ff-ae95-4e58399cee62", "product": {"name": "Linux", 